 "scenes": [
  {
   "id": "S01",
   "title": "End of life",
   "start": 0,
   "frames": 431,
   "target": 540,
   "scale": 0.7981,
   "vo": "On 7 April, Django 4.2 reached end of life. No more security fixes.",
   "voFile": "audio/vo/S01.mp3",
   "voSeconds": 6.18
  },
  {
   "id": "S02",
   "title": "Still shipped",
   "start": 431,
   "frames": 759,
   "target": 720,
   "scale": 1.0542,
   "vo": "But Debian 13 and Ubuntu 24.04 still ship it. Since then, Django has published 19 security advisories… and not one official patch for 4.2.",
   "voFile": "audio/vo/S02.mp3",
   "voSeconds": 11.65
  },
  {
   "id": "S03",
   "title": "The finding",
   "start": 1190,
   "frames": 1157,
   "target": 1200,
   "scale": 0.9642,
   "vo": "On October 1, Ubuntu shipped a backport for one of them. Five days later, Django said its original fix was incomplete. We took Ubuntu's source package, ran a test calibrated on Django's own fix commits… and the code path Django closed is still reachable in Ubuntu's build.",
   "voFile": "audio/vo/S03.mp3",
   "voSeconds": 18.29
  },
  {
   "id": "S04",
   "title": "Heirloom",
   "start": 2347,
   "frames": 573,
   "target": 660,
   "scale": 0.8682,
   "vo": "That test was run by Heirloom. An agent that keeps end-of-life software patched… and proves which old versions are actually vulnerable.",
   "voFile": "audio/vo/S04.mp3",
   "voSeconds": 8.55
  },
  {
   "id": "S05",
   "title": "The method",
   "start": 2920,
   "frames": 1080,
   "target": 1140,
   "scale": 0.9474,
   "vo": "Its first rule: never trust a test that hasn't failed. For each advisory, Heirloom writes its own test, proves it fails on Django's vulnerable code and passes on the fix… and only then asks the real question: is the old version affected?",
   "voFile": "audio/vo/S05.mp3",
   "voSeconds": 17
  },
  {
   "id": "S06",
   "title": "The campaign",
   "start": 4000,
   "frames": 1498,
   "target": 1680,
   "scale": 0.8917,
   "vo": "Then we let it run the whole campaign. 19 advisories, replayed in the order Django published them. 13 candidate backports, each proven by a test that fails before the fix and passes after. Where it couldn't prove something, it filed the evidence instead of guessing. And when a new fix amended one it had already backported, it stacked the follow-up on its own pull request.",
   "voFile": "audio/vo/S06.mp3",
   "voSeconds": 23.96
  },
  {
   "id": "S07",
   "title": "One question",
   "start": 5498,
   "frames": 926,
   "target": 1020,
   "scale": 0.9078,
   "vo": "Across the whole campaign, it asked me one question. A real judgement call, about changing Django's behaviour. I answered once. It sealed the answer as a precedent… and the next case reused it, without asking.",
   "voFile": "audio/vo/S07.mp3",
   "voSeconds": 14.44
  },
  {
   "id": "S08",
   "title": "Proof",
   "start": 6424,
   "frames": 1103,
   "target": 1380,
   "scale": 0.7993,
   "vo": "We tested the method on cases with known answers. A naive pipeline once called a vulnerable version safe. Heirloom? Zero times. Every claim in every pull request links to its neatlogs trace, and every backport links the Entire session of the agent that wrote it.",
   "voFile": "audio/vo/S08.mp3",
   "voSeconds": 17.39
  },
  {
   "id": "S09",
   "title": "Economics",
   "start": 7527,
   "frames": 666,
   "target": 660,
   "scale": 1.0091,
   "vo": "Each advisory cost about 20 cents of model time. We modelled the business in cfo.ai: what that's worth to the teams who keep old software alive.",
   "voFile": "audio/vo/S09.mp3",
   "voSeconds": 10.1
  },
  {
   "id": "S10",
   "title": "Kept honest",
   "start": 8193,
   "frames": 624,
   "target": 900,
   "scale": 0.6933,
   "vo": "Heirloom. Old software, kept honest. Every verdict is a test run you can open.",
   "voFile": "audio/vo/S10.mp3",
   "voSeconds": 6.004059
  }
 ],
